<title>USA: N.J. health agency $191 mln deal set for Aug 11 wk.</title>
<headline>N.J. health agency $191 mln deal set for Aug 11 wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New Jersey Health Care Facilities Financing Authority set the week of August 11 for a $191.07 million bond issue for Atlantic Health Systems, a source at Goldman Sachs &amp; Co, the senior manager, said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The deal received an A1 rating from Moody's, according to a statement from the rating agency.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
</text>
